2, "lead_after": -31.85, "points_lost": 3.86, "best": "B1"}, {"turn": 63, "color": "B", "move": "H1", "lead_before": -31.85, "lead_after": -35.8, "points_lost": 3.94, "best": "A9"}, {"turn": 64, "color": "W", "move": "F1", "lead_before": -35.8, "lead_after": -31.88, "points_lost": 3.92, "best": "B1"}, {"turn": 65, "color": "B", "move": "J2", "lead_before": -31.88, "lead_after": -35.68, "points_lost": 3.81, "best": "A9"}, {"turn": 66, "color": "W", "move": "J4", "lead_before": -35.68, "lead_after": -31.9, "points_lost": 3.78, "best": "B1"}], "review": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "title": "Four Leads Given Back, One Fatal Move at B4", "summary": "The 14k won as White when Opus 5.5 resigned on move 66's reply. Black held the lead several times: +7.1 after move 14, +8.0 after move 18, +10.8 after move 22 and +4.6 after move 50. Each time it gave the lead back, losing 3.5 points per move on average to the 14k's 2.6. The game was decided at move 51, when B4 dropped Black's lead from +4.6 to -45.4.", "moments": [{"turn": 14, "text": "White's H4 lost 7.8 points and moved Black's lead from -0.7 to +7.1. The engine preferred D6. Black was suddenly ahead after a quiet opening."}, {"turn": 15, "text": "Black answered with H3, which lost 6.9 points and sent the lead from +7.1 straight back to +0.2. The engine's choice was G5, the point White took next. The gift lasted exactly one move."}, {"turn": 18, "text": "White's J5 lost 9.7 points, the 14k's worst move of the game, and put Black at +8.0. The engine wanted C5. Opus 5.5 had another big lead and again let much of it slip, losing 3.1 points on C6 next."}, {"turn": 49, "text": "After White's A4 lost 8.8 points and put Black at +5.0, Opus 5.5 played B5 and lost 9.0 of them at once, falling to -4.0. The engine's choice was B8. The left side became a tangle of stones at the A-C files."}, {"turn": 51, "text": "B4 lost 49.9 points and turned +4.6 into -45.4, the move that decided the game. The engine's choice was B8, as it had been at turns 49 and 50. After this Black was never within 30 points again, and it resigned."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py only parses a pasted board and runs a flood fill to print each group's stones and liberty count, flagging groups with two or fewer liberties. It never generates, scores or ranks candidate moves and never looks ahead, so it only inspects the current position.", "stop": false}}